        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c679ef17b7c48a28e22c97b4f9e3f60",
      "statement": "JobQueue admits a job by inserting its Key into an OrdinalIgnoreCase in-flight dictionary before writing to an unbounded channel, rolls the key back if the write fails, and removes it in the per-job handler's finally block — so the key is held for the entire run and `false` from TryAdd means either that key is in flight or the queue is shutting down, never that the queue is full.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L14-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5665abe93b063377fbd07f5ea8012ae70dfbbaea3e069ce1af77587ab816a11:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L55-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed6c9811c63381075ba09fa23424fad593c738b9ffcf2b6ce880189842018a29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_000fcd492cb644beb407e872768aec33",
      "statement": "JobQueue executes jobs with Parallel.ForEachAsync under MaxConcurrentJobs = 10, gives each dequeued job its own async DI scope and shutdown-linked cancellation token, and isolates a non-cancellation exception to a single `Job {Key} failed` Error line without stopping the loop or retrying the job.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L41-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5586c73a9a67e6eac401a825f74689d10d926114316da1f624b2b1be6b9ebfca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3916b4ab89ae4f639b6e86c206ff1a75",
      "statement": "ImplementSpec.PrepareLock is a single static SemaphoreSlim shared by every job instance across all ten queue slots; it covers the entire preparation (fetch, mirror check, fast-forward, worktree creation) but is released before the agent runs, so agent runs proceed concurrently in their own worktrees while mirror operations are strictly serialized.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L23-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0576f1b593e9868ab2b453e66c149e20168af01fd386b5f8b9e124a0220ee8c7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L63-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1adcc5d278f63232d4ed568e5782aa0cd3c69d10eee1cd5850c4d89195203fc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c5853e1ddefa49b69416b7f3833ab014",
      "statement": "PrepareWorkspaceAsync runs, under the lock and in order: a check that Git.Repository is initialized, an OrdinalIgnoreCase cross-check of the issue's owner/repository against the parsed origin, `fetch --prune origin`, FindMirrorProblemAsync (throwing with its reason rather than degrading), an unconditional `merge --ff-only origin/main`, then layout at `<clone>/.sebastian/workspaces/<issueNumber>` on branch `sebastian/issue-<n>`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L63-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1adcc5d278f63232d4ed568e5782aa0cd3c69d10eee1cd5850c4d89195203fc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L153-L173",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81b2daf69aaa09e46e0e9a8016e58c6eb4e7737508cfe5c23914a8c00198e6ef:"
